Long ago, when the world was young, the Night Sky and the Earth were deeply in love. Each evening, the Sky would descend to embrace the Earth, covering her in starlit darkness. But as dawn approached, the Sun—jealous of their love—would chase the Night Sky away, forcing the lovers apart.

The Earth wept at this daily separation, her tears falling as she watched her beloved flee across the horizon. But the Night Sky, tender and wise, whispered a promise: "Though we must part each morning, I will leave you gifts to remember me by."

And so, each night when they embraced, the Night Sky wove his essence into tiny droplets of moisture, kissing every blade of grass, every leaf, and every flower. When morning came and he retreated, these crystalline tears remained—proof of their eternal devotion.

The Earth rejoiced at this gift. Now, every sunrise revealed millions of sparkling jewels scattered across her surface—morning dew, the Night Sky's love letters to the Earth.

This is why dew appears only in the early morning and quickly vanishes: it is the bittersweet remnant of their nightly reunion, evaporating as the jealous Sun reclaims the sky.

